; One channel of the frequency card, entered by hand.
FORM CHANNEL
TITLE Channel and frequency
SUMMARY Enters one channel of your frequency card by hand, for a region with no documents. The frequency is kept like an imported one and never shown again.
LEVEL ZERO
ORDER 40
ACTION channel_put
PREFILL channel name
FIELD name Designator(X) required upper max=12 check=designator
FIELD frequency Frequency(X) required secret check=frequency
FIELD unit Unit(KHZ,MHZ,HZ) default=KHZ
FIELD mode Mode(USB,LSB,ALE,DATA,AM,FM,CW) default=USB
FIELD use What it is for(X) upper max=40
FIELD ant_rx RX antenna, tuner port(1,2) default=1 fill
FIELD ant_tx TX antenna, tuner port(1,2) default=1 fill
NEXT CHANNEL SCHEDULE
BEGIN_HELP
Designator:
The name everyone uses for the channel, as on the card: P1, S1. Only the designator is ever sent in the clear.
END

Frequency:
As on the card. It is kept on this box and goes out only sealed to a checked member's card.
END

What it is for:
PRIMARY, SECONDARY, SCAN. No frequency here.
END

RX antenna, tuner port:
Tuner port this channel listens on, 1 or 2. Selected on a channel change, with RF off. Blank means 1.
END

TX antenna, tuner port:
Tuner port this channel transmits on, 1 or 2. The tuner switches to it before each transmit and back to RX after, with RF off. Tunes and tuner memories are on this port. Blank means 1.
END
